.TH "XmeMicroSleep" "library call"
.nh
.SH "NAME"
\fB\%XmeMicroSleep\fP \(em A widget writer function that waits for a number of microseconds
.iX "XmeMicroSleep"
.iX "Xme functions" "XmeMicroSleep"
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.PP
.nf
#include <Xm/XmP\&.h>
\fBint \fBXmeMicroSleep\fP\fR(
\fBlong \fBsecs\fR\fR);
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
\fB\%XmeMicroSleep\fP suspends the calling thread for \fIsecs\fP
microseconds, with \fB\%nanosleep\fP(2)\&.  Despite the name of the
argument, the time is in microseconds\&.
.IP "\fIsecs\fP" 10
Specifies the time to wait, in microseconds\&.
.PP
Motif 1\&.2 called this function \fB\%_XmMicroSleep\fP\&.  The library
still exports that name for old binaries, and \fB\%<Xm/XmP\&.h>\fP
defines it as a macro for \fB\%XmeMicroSleep\fP unless
\fB\%NO_XM_1_2_BC\fP is defined; new code should use
\fB\%XmeMicroSleep\fP\&.
.SH "RETURN"
.PP
Returns 0, or \-1 if the wait was interrupted by a signal (see
\fB\%nanosleep\fP(2))\&.
.SH "RELATED"
.PP
\fB\%nanosleep\fP(2)\&.
